    <blockquote>
    <h2>MariaDB Connector/Java 4.0.0</h2>
    <h2><a
    href="https://github.com/mariadb-corporation/mariadb-connector-j/tree/4.0.0">4.0.0</a>
    (Oct 2026)</h2>
    <p><a
    href="https://github.com/mariadb-corporation/mariadb-connector-j/compare/3.5.11...4.0.0">Full
    Changelog</a></p>
    <p>4.0.0 includes every fix of 3.5.11, listed below.</p>
    <h4>Major Changes</h4>
    <ul>
    <li>CONJ-1361 - Java 17 is the minimum runtime, Java 8 and 11 are no
    longer supported (the 3.5 branch remains available for Java 8)</li>
    <li>CONJ-1321 - TLS enabled by default: sslMode now defaults to
    verify-full</li>
    <li>CONJ-1384 - AWS IAM authentication moves to the separate artifact
    mariadb-java-client-aws, the connector no longer
    depends on the AWS SDK; the plugin gains STS assume role support
    (CONJ-877, report by Adrian Samatan) and ships
    the RDS root certificates so that the default sslMode validates an RDS
    endpoint without configuration</li>
    <li>CONJ-1306 - PreparedStatement.executeQuery() rejects statements that
    return no result set, as the JDBC
    specification requires; the permitNoResults option restores the former
    behavior (report by Christopher Schultz)</li>
    <li>CONJ-651 - Stream LOB columns from the socket instead of loading
    them in memory (report by Ilya Zhavoronkov)</li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Key Enhancements</h4>
    <ul>
    <li>CONJ-1386 - New sslMode=allow: verify-full when the server announces
    TLS, unencrypted otherwise, for a mix of
    servers with and without TLS behind one connection string</li>
    <li>CONJ-1347 - setSavepoint() throws in auto-commit mode instead of
    silently succeeding</li>
    <li>CONJ-1262 - cachedCodecs option now defaults to true</li>
    <li>CONJ-1370 - JNA dependency removed, Unix domain sockets use the JDK
    implementation</li>
    <li>CONJ-1371 - useReadAheadInput option and ReadAheadBufferedStream
    removed</li>
    <li>CONJ-1366 - First-class module-info.java (module
    org.mariadb.jdbc)</li>
    <li>CONJ-1367 - Virtual threads: no carrier pinning in driver locks,
    verified by a JFR-based test</li>
    <li>CONJ-1354 - GSSAPI authentication uses the native GSS-API where
    available</li>
    <li>CONJ-1308 - Support MariaDB 12.3 XML data type</li>
    <li>CONJ-1220 - Unix domain sockets on Windows, for SSH tunnels (report
    by DAIKOZ)</li>
    <li>CONJ-1378 - Try every IP address a hostname resolves to when opening
    the socket</li>
    <li>CONJ-1369 - Performance work on the Java 17 code base: packet reader
    and writer buffers, readNBytes, ranged
    Arrays.equals, no String.format on data paths</li>
    <li>CONJ-1365 - Performance: VarHandle little-endian access in packet
    buffers</li>
    <li>CONJ-1373 - Performance: JDK UTF-8 encoder for long strings in
    Writer.writeString / writeStringEscaped</li>
    <li>CONJ-1375 - Performance: cache codec resolution for getObject(index,
    Class) and setObject</li>
    <li>CONJ-1377 - Performance: faster client-side query parsing in
    ClientParser and NativeSql</li>
    <li>CONJ-1368 - Build and test tooling: tests run against the built jar,
    GraalVM metadata refreshed, CI matrix on
    Java 17, 21 and 25</li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Issues Resolved</h4>
    <ul>
    <li>CONJ-1383 - Connection init rebuilds session_track_system_variables
    from @<a href="https://github.com/global"><code>@​global</code></a>,
    discarding the session-level
    last_gtid set by MaxScale (report by Sawan Patel)</li>
    <li>CONJ-1379 - Set an explicit session tracking list and guard
    character_set_results like character_set_client
    (report by fg0x0)</li>
    <li>CONJ-1381 - Bound server-declared lengths by the packet before
    allocating and reading from them (report by fg0x0)</li>
    <li>CONJ-1374 - Redirect URL password partially logged when containing
    '@'</li>
    <li>CONJ-1372 - caching_sha2_password full authentication fails over a
    Unix socket when SSL is disabled (report by
    工藤航)</li>
    </ul>
